  "body": "What happens:\nThe test `disk_recovery::a_repaired_default_machine_file_is_read_again_through_the_disk_reader` fails on Windows. It is in `crates/app/tests/default_machine_missing/disk_recovery.rs` (from PR #4078, #2324). It passes on Linux and macOS.\n\nEvidence:\n- Windows quick check of main on host `bacon`, at `5c50f6721315`: one failure, this test.\n- Repeat on host `winnie`, at upstream main `a1c57b475`: `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test default_machine_missing`. 9 tests pass and this test fails:\n\n```\npanicked at crates\\app\\tests\\default_machine_missing\\disk_recovery.rs:60:5:\nthe reader must use the isolated folder: the default machine file 3axis-vmc.mch cannot be read (default machine:\n3axis-vmc.mch in C:\\Users\\...\\AppData\\Local\\Temp\\.tmpMvVxEv\\assets\\machines: The system cannot find the file\nspecified. (os error 2)) - mount a machine on the setup, or reinstall the file\n```\n\nCause:\nThe test makes the folder path with `join(\"assets/machines\")`. On Windows that gives `...\\.tmpXXXX\\assets/machines`, with a forward slash. The reader writes `...\\assets\\machines` in its message. The `missing.contains(machines.to_str())` check at line 60 then fails. The production reader is correct. Only the test is wrong.\n\nFix:\nMake the path with `join(\"assets\").join(\"machines\")` in the parent part and in `check_disk_recovery`. Do not change the reader.\n\nDone means:\n- The test passes on Windows (`bacon`, `lenny` or `winnie`) and still passes on Linux and macOS.\n- The test still refuses a reader that does not use the isolated folder.\n",
